 ("h2", "2.3 Continents"),
 ("p", "The number of continents depends on how we count — anywhere from **four to seven**. The reasons: North and South America can be seen as one landmass; Europe and Asia form one landmass (geologists call it **Eurasia**, though history and culture make them two); Africa and Eurasia can be joined as well."),
